WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.671
Every year on February 14th, couples, friends, and families in many countries give each other cards, chocolate, and candy.

2
00:00:10.672 --> 00:00:18.071
In fact over one billion cards are sent for this day, second only to Christmas.

3
00:00:18.072 --> 00:00:25.896
Children have big parties at school, families send each other cards, and couples might have romantic dinners.

4
00:00:25.897 --> 00:00:28.537
What do you do if you are single?

5
00:00:28.538 --> 00:00:32.236
Well Valentine's Day is not only for couples.

6
00:00:32.237 --> 00:00:35.372
It's about love, remember!

7
00:00:35.373 --> 00:00:38.468
Valentine's Day is your chance to be bold.

8
00:00:38.469 --> 00:00:42.033
Is there a girl or boy that you secretly like?

9
00:00:42.034 --> 00:00:44.475
Why not send them a valentine?

10
00:00:44.476 --> 00:00:50.530
A valentine is a card with a message inside, like a poem or love letter.

11
00:00:50.531 --> 00:00:56.258
You can decide if you want to sign your name or not.

12
00:00:56.259 --> 00:00:59.776
So where did the idea of Valentine's Day come from?

13
00:00:59.777 --> 00:01:06.934
In Italy about two thousand years ago, February 14th was a day to celebrate love.

14
00:01:06.935 --> 00:01:12.325
It was the day that the queen of the Roman gods, Juno, was honored.

15
00:01:12.326 --> 00:01:17.880
Juno was the god of women and marriage.

16
00:01:17.881 --> 00:01:23.662
Young Roman women each wrote their name on a piece of paper and put it in a big jar.

17
00:01:23.663 --> 00:01:26.786
Every young man in the town picked a name.

18
00:01:26.787 --> 00:01:31.252
Then the pairs were partners until the next February.

19
00:01:31.253 --> 00:01:34.973
Sometimes they married.

20
00:01:34.974 --> 00:01:39.504
At one time, however, young lovers in Italy could not marry.

21
00:01:39.505 --> 00:01:41.615
It was against the law!

22
00:01:41.616 --> 00:01:43.329
Why, you may ask?

23
00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:47.285
What could be wrong with people getting married?

24
00:01:47.286 --> 00:01:57.093
Emperor Claudius II, the head of the Roman Empire in 270 AD, needed a big army because he fought many wars.

25
00:01:57.094 --> 00:01:59.249
He did not have enough soldiers.

26
00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:06.074
He believed single men were better soldiers than married men.

27
00:02:06.075 --> 00:02:13.126
If you are married and have a family, you may not want to leave your country and fight in a distant land.

28
00:02:13.127 --> 00:02:20.422
If you are single, you may like to join the army for an adventure!

29
00:02:20.423 --> 00:02:26.558
Claudius needed more single men to be soldiers, and so he decided to outlaw marriage.

30
00:02:26.559 --> 00:02:29.786
People were angry, but they could do nothing.

31
00:02:29.787 --> 00:02:38.754
Claudius' nickname was Claudius the Cruel, and people who opposed him were usually killed.

32
00:02:38.755 --> 00:02:43.846
One brave priest, whose name was Valentine, did oppose the emperor.

33
00:02:43.847 --> 00:02:47.886
Father Valentine married couples secretly in his church.

34
00:02:47.887 --> 00:02:52.443
He married many happy couples until one day he was caught.

35
00:02:52.444 --> 00:02:56.227
The Roman guards took him away and threw him in a dungeon.

36
00:02:56.228 --> 00:03:02.110
Emperor Claudius ordered his death.

37
00:03:02.111 --> 00:03:06.730
While Valentine was in jail, he fell in love with the jailer's daughter.

38
00:03:06.731 --> 00:03:14.928
On the last day of his life, he sent her a love letter with the message, From your Valentine.

39
00:03:14.929 --> 00:03:25.351
In 489 AD, Father Valentine was made a saint by the Christian Church, and St. Valentine's Day was declared on February 14th.

40
00:03:25.352 --> 00:03:36.995
Father Valentine's message, From your Valentine, is still written in many Valentine's Day cards today, 1,500 years later!

41
00:03:36.996 --> 00:03:46.046
More importantly, Father Valentine's belief in the importance of love is still celebrated today between couples, families, and friends.

42
00:03:46.047 --> 00:03:49.959
Who will you send a valentine to?

